//? Title: Decoder KV Caching: Validated Appends and Absolute-Position Rebuilds
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
The exact upstream preparation protocol and the complete editable native C++ experiment preserve original source rows, seeds, fitting budgets and validation. Canonical components expose mathematical graphs; every objective, optimizer step, fitting/generation loop and deployment comparison remains visible.
)
\toc

> Replay every held-out position

The cache appends one key and value per head for each new token.
The causal query uses the accumulated prefix. The reference replay
checks all 2,048 held-out positions against a full-context evaluation
using the same native checkpoint, then generates 48 greedy tokens from
the first eight held-out tokens.

> Follow the actual data and model

New tokens / retained K,V -> causal chunk -> grown cache.

